// Constructs that pass type and borrow checking but the IL backend does not lower yet.
// Each must be reported as E0500: the backend never compiles them to placeholder IL.
// (`()`-typed struct fields and parameters were here until tuples and `()` values landed,
// decision 52; references to references and to `()` until `Ref<T>`, decision 64; arrays
// and slices of references until decision 77.)

// An inline array's length is an `int32` in the CLR.
fn Huge(_bytes: &[u8; 3000000000]) {} //~ ERROR E0500 an array of more than 2147483647 elements is not yet supported by code generation

fn Main() {}
